requirement of 1.0 water turnover per hour for the oldest cohorts, the main=
 RAS loop must process and deliver a continuous flow of approximately 448.8=
 cubic meters per hour (m=C2=B3/hr).</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"2,=
1,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"2,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Engineering St=
rategy (N+1 Redundancy):</b> In a closed Marine RAS, water flow is the prim=
ary life support. If flow stops, the biofilters crash and oxygen delivery c=
eases. The system requires a manifold of two identical heavy-duty marine ce=
ntrifugal pumps=E2=80=94each rated for 500 m=C2=B3/hr at low head (10=E2=80=
=9312 meters). One pump will act as the continuous duty drive, and the seco=
nd will serve as an automated standby.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"=
2,2,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"2,2,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">Infrastructu=
re Need:</b> 2x 22kW Marine-grade centrifugal pumps (Duplex Stainless or sp=
ecialized polymer), Variable Frequency Drives (VFDs) for flow scaling, a ma=
ster PLC controller, and the primary 150mm/200mm PVC/HDPE trunk lines routi=
ng from the sump through the filtration blocks and out to the raceways.</p>=
</li></ul><p data-path-to-node=3D"3"><b data-path-to-node=3D"3" data-index-=
in-node=3D"0">2. CAPEX Breakdown (AUD)</b></p><ul data-path-to-node=3D"4"><=
li><p data-path-to-node=3D"4,0,0">Primary Lift Pumps (2x 500 m=C2=B3/hr, 22=
kW Marine-grade centrifugal): $26,000</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"4=
,1,0">Master VFD Controllers &amp; PLC Integration (Automated duty-cycling =
