ndles it:</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"3"><b data-path-to-node=3D"3" data-ind=
ex-in-node=3D"0">1. Where your CO2 is currently being degassed:</b>
In our current financial model, you are actually getting a massive amount o=
f CO2 degassing "for free" through two systems:</p><ul data-path-to-node=3D=
"4"><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"4,0,0"><b data-path-to-node=3D"4,0,0" data-=
index-in-node=3D"0">The MBBR (Moving Bed Biofilm Reactor):</b> To tumble th=
e 30m=C2=B3 of K1 media, we costed four massive regenerative blowers. Pumpi=
ng that much atmospheric air through the water violently strips the dissolv=
ed CO2 out into the atmosphere.</p></li><li><p data-path-to-node=3D"4,1,0">=
<b data-path-to-node=3D"4,1,0" data-index-in-node=3D"0">The Protein Skimmer=
s (Fractionators):</b> These units use venturi pumps to whip air and water =
into a massive foam. This is one of the most efficient gas-exchange mechani=
sms in aquaculture, stripping residual CO2 while injecting ozone.</p></li><=
/ul><p data-path-to-node=3D"5"><b data-path-to-node=3D"5" data-index-in-nod=
e=3D"0">2. The "Calcium Reactor" Variable:</b>
Because we just added the Aragonite Calcium Reactor to your design, you hav=
e a new source of CO2. Calcium reactors work by injecting pure CO2 into a c=
hamber of water to make it acidic enough to melt the dead coral. The water =
exiting that reactor is loaded with dissolved calcium, but it is also <i da=
ta-path-to-node=3D"5" data-index-in-node=3D"330">loaded with excess CO2</i>=
.</p><p data-path-to-node=3D"6"><b data-path-to-node=3D"6" data-index-in-no=
